        "student_prefix_sha256": "2e5b21ac0a7f46a7c970b788c9f764a4ba41048545087e42ac1a15e9ba361506",
        "target": "First, I identify the given quantities:\n- James invests $2000 a week.\n- He starts with $250,000.\n- There are 52 weeks in a year.\n\nNext, I calculate the total amount James invests in a year:\n\\[ 2000 \\times 52 = 104,000 \\]\n\nThen, I add this to his initial amount:\n\\[ 250,000 + 104,000 = 354,000 \\]\n\nAt the end of the year, he gets a windfall that is 50% more than what he has in his bank account:\n\\[ 354,000 \\times 1.5 = 531,000 \\]\n\nFinally, I add the windfall to his account balance:\n\\[ 354,000 + 531,000 = 885,000 \\]\n\nFINAL: 885000",
